"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Can a linear probe read Lean autoformalization drift from generator activations, and does synthetic-drift training transfer to human-audited natural misformalizations?\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"Generators encode drift they cannot verbalize: a linear probe predicts trace correctness at 0.953, so Lean misformalizations should be linearly readable.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:sequential_part\",\"text\":\"Expert-labelled faithful/drifted pairs, one forward pass per statement, probe fit, held-out evaluation — four steps.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:method\",\"text\":\"Synthetic drift is generated in parallel by counterfactual perturbation, and forward passes over many statements run side-by-side on separate GPUs.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"Synthetic-drift probes transfer to natural Lean misformalizations: parallel GPUs reach AUROC ≥ 0.80 at 5,000 statement-runs, sooner than one sequential GPU.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Drift is weakly readable in Lean: probe AUROC on natural misformalizations stays near 0.679 even at 150,000 statement-runs, so it never crosses the flagging threshold.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Cache a 7B Lean autoformalizer's hidden states over 100k+ runs; train logistic probes on synthetic drift, test on 200 human-audited natural misformalizations; time parallel 4-GPU vs sequential and sharded-copy baselines; compare AUROC to SMT-LIB 0.960/0.679.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"A linear SAE probe reached 0.960 AUROC against an SMT-LIB solver oracle but 0.679 against intent labels; largest compute: 950 encodings, one 27B verifier.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_genv_oracle\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.11085v2\",\"quote\":\"A linear probe on the sparse features recovers 0.960 AUROC for GenV+HN.\"}],\"value\":950}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"No one has measured drift readability in Lean (only SMT-LIB), scored a probe against human audit labels, or tested synthetic-to-natural drift transfer.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Planted synthetic-drift probe hits AUROC ≥ 0.90; 4-shard parallel caching matches single-GPU sequential caching within ±0.05 AUROC; shuffle control 0.50.\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_genv_oracle\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.11085v2\",\"quote\":\"A linear probe on the sparse features recovers 0.960 AUROC for GenV+HN.\"}],\"value\":0.96}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Shows readability, not a causal fix, and only within Lean. Cannot prove synthetic-to-natural transfer beyond the audited 200 pairs.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:s_genv_oracle\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2609.11085v2\",\"quote\":\"A linear probe on the sparse features recovers 0.960 AUROC for GenV+HN.\",\"supports\":\"smt_probe_auroc_oracle; baseline; anchor published value\"}

